# Code owners for harbourspace-org/claude-marketplace.
#
# Every path resolves to @harbourspace-org/devs — the org has one team today, so
# this is a declaration of ownership rather than a routing rule. It exists for
# two reasons:
#
#   1. `require_code_owner_review` in a branch ruleset is inert without owners
#      declared here. This repo has no ruleset yet; when it gets one, the file
#      is already in place and the rule bites immediately.
#   2. `.github/` is explicitly owned. The Claude GitHub App is installed on
#      this org with `workflows:write`, so an agent working from Slack can edit
#      CI. Owning the path means a human signs off on a change to it.
#
# CODEOWNERS is read from the BASE branch of a pull request, so this applies to
# PRs into `main`. Copy it to any other long-lived branch that takes PRs.

*           @harbourspace-org/devs
/.github/   @harbourspace-org/devs
